IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pr77-nouns`
IMPORT `pr77-cross-references`

-- Row il-77. TESTS THAT PIN THE READINGS of the two items: the issue dates the footers print, the series and number of each issue, what each instruction names and does, the words each printed text holds, the commencements as the pages print them, and both limbs of each item with how each was read.
-- These pass: they say what was read from what. The assertions that the references are NOT complete are in pr77-tests-red.l4.
-- The expected values are written from NOTES.md (the answer tables and the quotation lines), not copied from the values in pr77-cross-references.l4.

§ `Tests of the readings`

-- The issue dates the footers print. An issue date is NOT a commencement date.
#ASSERT `the 1965 issue`'s `its issue date` EQUALS Date 1 8 1965
#ASSERT `SH 2029`'s `its issue date` EQUALS Date 6 9 2005
#ASSERT `SH 2333`'s `its issue date` EQUALS Date 23 1 2012
#ASSERT `SH 2980`'s `its issue date` EQUALS Date 27 6 2022
#ASSERT `KT 10534`'s `its issue date` EQUALS Date 26 1 2023
#ASSERT `SH 2042`'s `its issue date` EQUALS Date 26 12 2005
#ASSERT `SH 2173`'s `its issue date` EQUALS Date 30 7 2008
#ASSERT `SH 1766`'s `its issue date` EQUALS Date 25 12 2000
#ASSERT `SH 1030`'s `its issue date` EQUALS Date 15 6 1981

-- The series, and what is certain about the issue number. The footer of the 1965 issue prints the number 466 on the best reading, and its last digit is not certain in the scan.
#ASSERT `the 1965 issue`'s `its series` EQUALS `Sefer HaChukim`
#ASSERT `KT 10534`'s `its series` EQUALS `Kovetz HaTakanot`
#ASSERT `the 1965 issue`'s `its issue number` EQUALS 466
#ASSERT NOT (`the 1965 issue`'s `the last digit of its issue number is certain in the scan`)
#ASSERT `SH 2029`'s `the last digit of its issue number is certain in the scan`
#ASSERT `SH 2980`'s `the last digit of its issue number is certain in the scan`
#ASSERT `SH 2042`'s `the last digit of its issue number is certain in the scan`
#ASSERT `SH 2173`'s `the last digit of its issue number is certain in the scan`

-- The order of the instruments item I1 rests on, by issue date.
#ASSERT `the first instrument was issued after the second` `SH 2333` `SH 2029`
#ASSERT `the first instrument was issued after the second` `SH 2980` `SH 2333`
#ASSERT `the first instrument was issued after the second` `KT 10534` `SH 2980`
#ASSERT NOT (`the first instrument was issued after the second` `the 1965 issue` `SH 2029`)

-- I1: what each instruction does, and where. Each inserts one paragraph label of section 2(א), directly after the label it names.
#ASSERT `SH 2029 section 8 inserts paragraph (11 alef)`'s `the kind` EQUALS Insert
#ASSERT `SH 2029 section 8 inserts paragraph (11 alef)`'s `the place it names` EQUALS `section 2(alef) of the Law`
#ASSERT `SH 2029 section 8 inserts paragraph (11 alef)`'s `the printed page it is on` EQUALS 998
#ASSERT `SH 2333 section 2 inserts paragraph (11 bet)`'s `the kind` EQUALS Insert
#ASSERT `SH 2333 section 2 inserts paragraph (11 bet)`'s `the place it names` EQUALS `section 2(alef) of the Law`
#ASSERT `SH 2333 section 2 inserts paragraph (11 bet)`'s `the label it inserts` EQUALS JUST `label (11 bet)`
#ASSERT `SH 2333 section 2 inserts paragraph (11 bet)`'s `the printed page it is on` EQUALS 142
#ASSERT `SH 2980 section 10(2) inserts paragraph (11 gimel)`'s `the kind` EQUALS Insert
#ASSERT `SH 2980 section 10(2) inserts paragraph (11 gimel)`'s `the place it names` EQUALS `section 2(alef) of the Law`
#ASSERT `SH 2980 section 10(2) inserts paragraph (11 gimel)`'s `it comes after the label` EQUALS JUST `label (11 bet)`
#ASSERT `SH 2980 section 10(2) inserts paragraph (11 gimel)`'s `the label it inserts` EQUALS JUST `label (11 gimel)`
#ASSERT `SH 2980 section 10(2) inserts paragraph (11 gimel)`'s `the printed page it is on` EQUALS 882

-- I1: what the instructions put in, as the pages print it, and the opening of section 2(א).
#ASSERT `SH 2029 section 8 inserts paragraph (11 alef)`'s `the words it puts` EQUALS LIST "כתובת למשלוח דואר כמשמעותה בחוק עדכון כתובת, התשס״ה–2005, ככל שנמסרה על כך הודעה;"
#ASSERT `SH 2980 section 10(2) inserts paragraph (11 gimel)`'s `the words it puts` EQUALS LIST "המען הדיגיטלי;"
#ASSERT `the printed text contains the words` `the opening line of section 2(alef) as printed in 1965` "יירשמו הפרטים הבאים"

-- I1: the order of section 2(א) from (9) to (13) after the instructions whose commencement is established from a page: (11א) and (11ב) lie between (9) and (13). The instruction of SH 2980 is not in that order.
#ASSERT `the labels after the instructions whose commencement is established` EQUALS LIST `label (9)`, `label (10)`, `label (11)`, `label (11 alef)`, `label (11 bet)`, `label (12)`, `label (13)`
#ASSERT NOT (elem `label (11 gimel)` `the labels after the instructions whose commencement is established`)
#ASSERT `the labels from a to b` `label (9)` `label (13)` `the labels after the instructions whose commencement is established` EQUALS LIST `label (9)`, `label (10)`, `label (11)`, `label (11 alef)`, `label (11 bet)`, `label (12)`, `label (13)`

-- I1: the commencements as the pages print them. SH 2029 prints a calendar date, which is not its issue date. SH 2333 and SH 2980 print periods and no calendar date. KT 10534 prints a limit.
#ASSERT `the commencement of SH 2029 section 9`'s `the date the page prints` EQUALS JUST (Date 1 2 2006)
#ASSERT NOT (`the commencement of SH 2029 section 9`'s `the date the page prints` EQUALS JUST (`SH 2029`'s `its issue date`))
#ASSERT `the commencement of SH 2029 section 9`'s `how it was read` EQUALS `official page image`
#ASSERT `the commencement of SH 2333 section 4`'s `the date the page prints` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the commencement of SH 2333 section 4`'s `the period the page prints` EQUALS JUST (`A printed period` WITH `its count` IS 4.5, `its unit` IS Months)
#ASSERT `the commencement of SH 2333 section 4`'s `how it was read` EQUALS `printed as a period, no calendar date computed`
#ASSERT (`the commencement of SH 2980 section 19(1)`'s `the commencement as read`)'s `the date the page prints` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`the commencement of SH 2980 section 19(1)`'s `the commencement as read`)'s `the period the page prints` EQUALS JUST (`A printed period` WITH `its count` IS 7, `its unit` IS Months)
#ASSERT `the commencement of SH 2980 section 19(1)`'s `an earlier notice in Reshumot can end the period`
#ASSERT `the commencement of SH 2980 section 19(1)`'s `the longest extension by order the page prints` EQUALS `A printed period` WITH `its count` IS 6, `its unit` IS Months
#ASSERT `the commencement of SH 2980 section 19(1)`'s `the printed page it is on` EQUALS 889
#ASSERT `the order of KT 10534`'s `the limit the page prints` EQUALS Date 27 6 2023
#ASSERT `the order of KT 10534`'s `an earlier notice in Reshumot can end it`
#ASSERT NOT (`the order of KT 10534`'s `it names a section of the Population Registry Law`)
#ASSERT `the order of KT 10534`'s `the printed page it is on` EQUALS 962

-- I1: the commencement of paragraph (11ג) is not established from a page. It is typed with no date and no period, and it is the only one of the three that is not established.
#ASSERT `the commencement of paragraph (11 gimel)`'s `how it was read` EQUALS `not established from a page`
#ASSERT `the commencement of paragraph (11 gimel)`'s `the date the page prints` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the commencement of paragraph (11 gimel)`'s `the period the page prints` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`the commencement is established from a page` `the commencement of paragraph (11 gimel)`)
#ASSERT `the commencement is established from a page` `the commencement of SH 2029 section 9`
#ASSERT `the commencement is established from a page` `the commencement of SH 2333 section 4`
#ASSERT (`SH 2980 section 10(2) inserts paragraph (11 gimel)`'s `the commencement as read`)'s `how it was read` EQUALS `not established from a page`

-- I1: limb (b). No instruction deposited here on the Law names section 3. Whether an instrument not read does is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY (NOTES.md).
#ASSERT NOT (any (GIVEN i YIELD (i's `the place it names`)'s `its section` EQUALS 3) `the instructions deposited here on the Law`)
#ASSERT all (GIVEN i YIELD (i's `the place it names`)'s `its law` EQUALS `the Population Registry Law`) `the instructions deposited here on the Law`

-- I1: the item, both limbs, and how each was read.
#ASSERT `both limbs hold` `item I1: section 3 points at (9) to (13) of section 2, and three paragraphs were inserted between those labels`
#ASSERT `item I1: section 3 points at (9) to (13) of section 2, and three paragraphs were inserted between those labels`'s `limb (a) was read` EQUALS `official page image`
#ASSERT `item I1: section 3 points at (9) to (13) of section 2, and three paragraphs were inserted between those labels`'s `limb (b) was read` EQUALS `official page images, completeness CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`

-- I2: what SH 2042 does and where, the commencement it prints, and the words of the paragraph it writes.
#ASSERT `SH 2042 section 1 marks and adds after in section 6`'s `the kind` EQUALS `Mark and add after`
#ASSERT `SH 2042 section 1 marks and adds after in section 6`'s `the place it names` EQUALS `section 6 of the Law`
#ASSERT `SH 2042 section 1 marks and adds after in section 6`'s `the printed page it is on` EQUALS 106
#ASSERT `paragraph (2) of subsection 6(gimel) as printed in SH 2042`'s `the place it is printed at` EQUALS `paragraph (2) of subsection 6(gimel) of the Law`
#ASSERT `the printed text contains the words` `paragraph (2) of subsection 6(gimel) as printed in SH 2042` "לחוק מידע גנטי, התשס״א–2000"
#ASSERT `the pointers in paragraph 6(gimel)(2)`'s `the place that pointer names` EQUALS `subsection 3(dalet) of the Genetic Information Law`
#ASSERT (`the pointers in paragraph 6(gimel)(2)`'s `the place that pointer names`)'s `its law` EQUALS `the Genetic Information Law`
#ASSERT `the commencement of SH 2042 section 3`'s `the period the page prints` EQUALS JUST (`A printed period` WITH `its count` IS 30, `its unit` IS Days)
#ASSERT `the commencement of SH 2042 section 3`'s `the date the page prints` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the commencement of SH 2042 section 3`'s `how it was read` EQUALS `printed as a period, no calendar date computed`

-- I2: the target as SH 1766 printed it: the definition on page 62, and subsection (ד) of section 3 on page 63.
#ASSERT `the definition of the term as printed in SH 1766`'s `the printed page it is on` EQUALS 62
#ASSERT `subsection 3(dalet) as printed in SH 1766`'s `the printed page it is on` EQUALS 63
#ASSERT `subsection 3(dalet) as printed in SH 1766`'s `the place it is printed at` EQUALS `subsection 3(dalet) of the Genetic Information Law`
#ASSERT (`the definition of the term as printed in SH 1766`'s `the place it is printed at`)'s `the term it defines` EQUALS JUST "בדיקה גנטית להורות"

-- I2: what SH 2173 does and where. Its section 2 prints בטל for the subsection the citing words name; its section 1(1) prints a definition in place of the one named.
#ASSERT `SH 2173 section 2 marks subsection 3(dalet) void`'s `the kind` EQUALS `Marked as void`
#ASSERT `SH 2173 section 2 marks subsection 3(dalet) void`'s `the place it names` EQUALS `subsection 3(dalet) of the Genetic Information Law`
#ASSERT `SH 2173 section 2 marks subsection 3(dalet) void`'s `the place it names` EQUALS `the pointers in paragraph 6(gimel)(2)`'s `the place that pointer names`
#ASSERT `SH 2173 section 2 marks subsection 3(dalet) void`'s `the words it puts` EQUALS LIST "בטל"
#ASSERT `SH 2173 section 2 marks subsection 3(dalet) void`'s `the printed page it is on` EQUALS 736
#ASSERT `SH 2173 section 1(1) prints a definition in place of the one named`'s `the kind` EQUALS `Replace definition`
#ASSERT `SH 2173 section 1(1) prints a definition in place of the one named`'s `the place it names` EQUALS `section 2 of the Genetic Information Law, the definition of the term`
#ASSERT `SH 2173 section 1(1) prints a definition in place of the one named`'s `the words it puts` EQUALS LIST "״בדיקה גנטית לקשרי משפחה״ – בדיקה גנטית לקביעת ממצאים בדבר קשרי משפחה של אדם;"
#ASSERT `SH 2173 section 1(1) prints a definition in place of the one named`'s `the printed page it is on` EQUALS 736
#ASSERT `the commencement of SH 2173 section 8`'s `the period the page prints` EQUALS JUST (`A printed period` WITH `its count` IS 4, `its unit` IS Months)
#ASSERT `the commencement of SH 2173 section 8`'s `the date the page prints` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the commencement of SH 2173 section 8`'s `how it was read` EQUALS `printed as a period, no calendar date computed`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN i YIELD (i's `the place it names`)'s `its section` EQUALS 3) `the instructions deposited here that touch section 3 of the Genetic Information Law`

-- I2: item 2a, as the page prints it. The row does not rest on these words.
#ASSERT `SH 2173 section 5 inserts a chapter whose first section is 28 alef`'s `the place it names` EQUALS `section 28(alef) of the Genetic Information Law`
#ASSERT `SH 2173 section 5 inserts a chapter whose first section is 28 alef`'s `the printed page it is on` EQUALS 736
#ASSERT `section 28 alef as printed in SH 2173`'s `the place it is printed at` EQUALS `section 28(alef) of the Genetic Information Law`
#ASSERT `the printed text contains the words` `section 28 alef as printed in SH 2173` "לא תיערך בדיקה גנטית לקשרי משפחה"

-- I2: the Interpretation Law as SH 1030 printed it. The words are typed as printed, and the tests pin only where each was printed and how each begins.
#ASSERT `section 1 of the Interpretation Law as printed in SH 1030`'s `the printed page it is on` EQUALS 302
#ASSERT `section 25 of the Interpretation Law as printed in SH 1030`'s `the printed page it is on` EQUALS 305
#ASSERT (`section 1 of the Interpretation Law as printed in SH 1030`'s `the place it is printed at`)'s `its law` EQUALS `the Interpretation Law`
#ASSERT `the printed text contains the words` `section 1 of the Interpretation Law as printed in SH 1030` "חוק זה יחול לגבי כל חיקוק והוראת מינהל"
#ASSERT `the printed text contains the words` `section 25 of the Interpretation Law as printed in SH 1030` "אזכור של חיקוק בחיקוק אחר"

-- I2: the item, both limbs, and how each was read.
#ASSERT `both limbs hold` `item I2: section 6(gimel)(2) points at subsection 3(dalet) of the Genetic Information Law, and SH 2173 prints the word for void against that subsection`
#ASSERT `item I2: section 6(gimel)(2) points at subsection 3(dalet) of the Genetic Information Law, and SH 2173 prints the word for void against that subsection`'s `limb (a) was read` EQUALS `official page image`
#ASSERT `item I2: section 6(gimel)(2) points at subsection 3(dalet) of the Genetic Information Law, and SH 2173 prints the word for void against that subsection`'s `limb (b) was read` EQUALS `official page images, completeness CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
